* PCC precharge/discharge simulation models (ngspice)
* Behavioral models built from the part datasheets. Values marked TUNE
* are not on the datasheet and are estimates.

* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* K1: Rincon RH3-12V, SPDT HV relay (datasheet REV B)
*   coil 80 ohm, pick-up 8 V max (100 mA), drop-out 0.5-5 V (6-62 mA)
*   operate 6 ms max, release 6 ms max, contact R 20 mohm max
* Contacts follow coil CURRENT, so dropout includes the
* L/R decay through the flyback diode, plus the mechanical delay.
*   pins: A1 A2 = coil, COM = 11, NC = 12, NO = 14
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt RELAY_SPDT A1 A2 COM NC NO
Rcoil A1 n1 80
* coil inductance is not on the datasheet  (TUNE)
Lcoil n1 n2 100m
Vsense n2 A2 0
* pick-up <= 100 mA, drop-out 6-62 mA: one smooth threshold at 65 mA
* (a hysteresis switch here chatters at small time steps)
Bdet det 0 V = 5 + 5*tanh((I(Vsense)-65m)/2m)
* 6 ms operate / release: RC crossing 5 V at tau*ln2
Rdly det cd 8.66k
Cdly cd 0 1u
S1 COM NO cd 0 SWNO
S2 COM NC cd 0 SWNC
.model SWNO sw vt=5 vh=0.1 ron=20m roff=100Meg
.model SWNC sw vt=5 vh=0.1 ron=100Meg roff=20m
.ends RELAY_SPDT

* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* AIR: Rincon REC45B1JA, SPST-NO HV contactor, integrated PWM economizer
*   coil "J": 9-36 V, pick-up 9 V max, drop-out 6 V min
*   inrush 3.8 A max for 130 ms max (3.2 ohm coil), hold 0.17 A at 12 V
*   operate 25 ms max, release 10 ms max, contact R 0.15 mohm typ
* The economizer electronics are modeled as a current draw, not an
* inductor: inrush = V/3.2 for 130 ms, then constant 2.04 W hold.
*   pins: A1 A2 = coil, COM = 13, NO = 14
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt AIR A1 A2 COM NO
Rleak A1 A2 10k
* economizer under-voltage lockout: on above 9 V, off below 6 V
Vrail rail 0 10
Evin vin 0 A1 A2 1
S0 rail pw vin 0 SWUV
Rpw pw 0 1k
.model SWUV sw vt=7.5 vh=1.5 ron=1 roff=1G
Epw pwb 0 pw 0 1
* 130 ms inrush timer, reset whenever the coil drops out
Rtm pwb tmr 187.5k
Ctm tmr 0 1u
Stm tmr 0 0 pwb SWRST
.model SWRST sw vt=-5 vh=0.1 ron=10 roff=1G
Bcoil A1 A2 I = (V(pwb)/10) * (V(tmr) < 5 ? V(A1,A2)/3.2 : 2.04/max(V(A1,A2),6))
* contacts: 25 ms operate, 10 ms release
* charge through Rop (tau 36 ms); discharge also through Drel + Rrel (tau 14 ms)
Rop pwb cd 36.1k
Drel cd nrel DREL
Rrel nrel pwb 24k
.model DREL D(is=1e-14)
Ccd cd 0 1u
S1 COM NO cd 0 SWC
.model SWC sw vt=5 vh=0.1 ron=1m roff=100Meg
.ends AIR

* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* IRLZ44N, logic-level N-MOSFET, 55 V / 47 A
* Generic VDMOS fit (Vth ~1.8 V, Rds(on) ~25 mohm at Vgs = 3.3-5 V,
* Ciss ~1.7 nF, 55 V body-diode breakdown). Replace with Infineon's
* model for accurate switching edges.
*   pins: D G S
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.model IRLZ44N VDMOS(Vto=1.8 Kp=50 Lambda=0.003 Rd=8m Rs=6m Rg=3
+ Cgdmax=1.5n Cgdmin=60p A=0.5 Cgs=1.6n
+ Is=2e-12 N=1 Cjo=1.1n Vj=0.8 M=0.5 Tt=80n Bv=55)
